      },
      "justification": "End-tidal CO2 monitoring should be applied to confirm endotracheal tube placement if intubated, assess CPR quality (target ETCO2 >10 mmHg), and detect ROSC (sudden rise in ETCO2). Given suspected opioid involvement, monitoring ventilation quality is important."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "continue_high_quality_cpr",
      "timestamp_minutes": 30.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "Per AHA ACLS guidelines, high-quality CPR must be maintained continuously during cardiac arrest. This is a required action for asystole/PEA management and must not be interrupted."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "evaluate_reversible_causes",
      "timestamp_minutes": 35.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "AHA ACLS guidelines require evaluation of reversible causes (H's and T's) for asystole/PEA. With suspected opioid use as a comorbidity, opioid toxicity is a potentially reversible cause that must be identified and treated."
    },
    {
